      "text": "To solve the problem \\(\\frac{235^2 - 221^2}{14}\\), we can use the difference of squares formula, which states that \\(a^2 - b^2 = (a - b)(a + b)\\). Here, \\(a = 235\\) and \\(b = 221\\).\n\nFirst, apply the difference of squares formula:\n\\[\n235^2 - 221^2 = (235 - 221)(235 + 221)\n\\]\n\nCalculate the differences and sums:\n\\[\n235 - 221 = 14\n\\]\n\\[\n235 + 221 = 456\n\\]\n\nNow substitute these values back into the expression:\n\\[\n235^2 - 221^2 = 14 \\times 456\n\\]\n\nNext, multiply 14 by 456:\n\\[\n14 \\times 456 = 14 \\times (400 + 56) = 14 \\times 400 + 14 \\times 56\n\\]\n\\[\n14 \\times 400 = 5600\n\\]\n\\[\n14 \\times 56 = 784\n\\]\n\nAdd these results together:\n\\[\n5600 + 784 = 6384\n\\]\n\nNow, we need to divide by 14:\n\\[\n\\frac{235^2 - 221^2}{14} = \\frac{6384}{14}\n\\]\n\nPerform the division:\n\\[\n\\frac{6384}{14} = 456\n\\]\n\nThus, the value is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{456}\n\\]",
